Color-coding rule: assign one faculty hue per academic unit; render the unit's `card-college-tile` accent rule and `badge-faculty` chip in that hue, but keep the unit page's masthead, CTAs, and body on the core maroon/ink system. Never run two faculty hues against each other as a primary scheme.

## Iteration Guide

1. Focus on ONE component at a time; resist refactoring an entire section in one pass
2. Reference component names and tokens directly (`{colors.primary}`, `{typography.display-xxl}`, `{rounded.xl}`, `mosaic-band`, `emblem-lockup`) — do not paraphrase to hex/px in prose
3. Run `npx @google/design.md lint DESIGN.md` after edits — `broken-ref`, `contrast-ratio`, and `orphaned-tokens` warnings flag issues automatically
4. Add new variants as separate component entries (`-pressed`, `-disabled`, `-focused`); never bury state inside prose
5. Default body to `{typography.body-md}`; reach for `{typography.body-emphasis}` for run-in bolds; keep display sizes for true heading roles
6. Keep `{colors.primary}` scarce and the emblem/wordmark sacred — the maroon masthead + one CTA + the mosaic seam is enough signal per viewport; the calligraphic wordmark and 校徽 are fixed assets, never redrawn
7. When introducing a new section band, choose from `{colors.canvas}` / `{colors.cloud}` / `{colors.fog}` / `{colors.charcoal-band}` / `{colors.primary}` — five pre-defined surface modes are the entire surface vocabulary
8. Treat the `mosaic-band` as a brand artifact, not a texture: anchor it to an edge, seam, banner-tip, or hero field on the modular grid — never tile it behind running text
